# ArcheFlow in Cursor

ArcheFlow is a set of skills (Markdown instructions) plus Bash helpers in `lib/`. In Cursor
the core skills are loaded through three adapters in `.cursor/skills/`:

| Command | Adapter | Core skill |
|---------|---------|------------|
| `/archeflow-review` | `.cursor/skills/archeflow-review/` | `skills/review/SKILL.md` |
| `/archeflow-run <task>` | `.cursor/skills/archeflow-run/` | `skills/run/SKILL.md` |
| `/archeflow-sprint` | `.cursor/skills/archeflow-sprint/` | `skills/sprint/SKILL.md` |

For the other functions, read the core skill and follow it: `skills/init/`, `skills/status/`,
`skills/report/`, `skills/dag/`, `skills/replay/`, `skills/score/`, `skills/memory/`,
`skills/scan/` (the Claude Code names are `/archeflow:<name>`).

## Agents

Where a skill spawns `archeflow:<role>`, use
`Task(subagent_type="generalPurpose", prompt="<full text of agents/<role>.md>\n\n---\n\n<prompt>")`.
Spawn parallel reviewers as several `Task` calls in one message. Give each agent only the
inputs the skill lists for its role.

## Scripts

Call `lib/archeflow-*.sh` with the Shell tool from the project root, using the absolute path of
the ArcheFlow checkout. They need Bash 4+, jq 1.6+ and git. Never paste task text or agent
output into a shell command; write it to a file first, as the skills describe.

## Skip ArcheFlow

For single-line fixes, questions, reading code, config tweaks and plain git operations.
